Order is minus the OLS slope of ln(error) on ln(n), using absolute error > 10⁻¹⁵. Intervals use Student t with m−2 degrees of freedom; they describe regression uncertainty, not independent stochastic measurement error. Interval endpoints rounded to six or nine decimals can conceal small deviations from theory; full precision is retained in orders.csv. Simpson uses a midpoint per panel (2n subintervals).
